### 1.5 SaaS Gaps & Industry Standard Shortcomings (P1 - P3)

#### 🟠 Gap 17: Synchronous Long-Running HTTP Requests (Missing Job Queue)
- Multi-cycle simulation pipelines (3 to 10 cycles with multiple scenarios and LLM invocations) take 30 to 180 seconds.
- Synchronously blocking `POST /pipeline` causes HTTP 504 gateway timeouts across reverse proxies (Nginx, Cloudflare).
- **Industry Standard:** Asynchronous worker queue (BullMQ + Redis). Return `202 Accepted` with a `job_id`, providing real-time status streaming via WebSockets or Server-Sent Events (SSE).

#### 🟠 Gap 18: Complete Absence of AuthN / AuthZ & Multi-Tenancy
- Zero authentication exists. Anyone can trigger arbitrary C++ process spawns and consume LLM API quotas.
- Missing tenant/workspace isolation, API key management for programmatic access, and Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).

#### 🟠 Gap 19: Missing Request Validation & Rate Limiting
- No payload validation (Zod / Joi). Unsanitized inputs can cause crashes or NoSQL injection vulnerabilities.
- Missing `express-rate-limit` to prevent DoS attacks against high-cost simulation endpoints.

#### 🟠 Gap 20: Non-Functional Frontend Prototype
- [`home.jsx`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/MOP-Simulator/frontend/src/app/page/home.jsx) form has zero React state or event listeners.
- "Run Simulation" button does nothing; results display is an unpopulated placeholder.
- [`main.jsx`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/MOP-Simulator/frontend/src/app/components/home/main.jsx) and [`footer.jsx`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/MOP-Simulator/frontend/src/app/components/home/footer.jsx) are 0-byte blank files.
- The 740KB Three.js visualizer is trapped in an external static HTML file rather than embedded natively in Next.js.

#### 🟡 Gap 21: Platform Binary Portability
- [`simulationRunner.js`](file:///c:/Users/Omid/X/Code/MOP-Simulator/backend/src/Automation/versionOne/service/simulationRunner.js#L24) hardcodes `bin/mop_sim.exe`. Fails immediately when deployed on Linux or containerized environments.

